Source works
------------

This dataset unifies and digitises material from public-domain reference
works:

- Nave's Topical Bible (1896), by Orville J. Nave — public domain by age.
- Torrey's New Topical Textbook (1897), by R. A. Torrey — public domain
  by age.

The pilot enrichment layer (`data/03_pilot`) additionally carries
definitions drawn from two further public-domain works, sourced from the
sibling `bible-dictionary-dataset` repository:

- Easton's Bible Dictionary (1897), by Matthew George Easton — public
  domain by age.
- Smith's Bible Dictionary (1863), by William Smith — public domain by
  age.

Digitisation of the original XML source texts is credited to the
Christian Classics Ethereal Library (CCEL, https://www.ccel.org/).

The public-domain status of the source works does not attach to their
CCEL digitisation, or to this project's parsing, unification, and AI
enrichment work, which are original contributions offered under CC BY
4.0 above.

See README.md for the full source table and per-layer provenance.
